    "aspectRules": {
      "9:16": "The 9:16 map is a set of anchors, not stretch boxes. Background plates may bleed and use cover; character, prop and diorama plates use contain and are re-staged, never cropped. Text auto-fits inside; top-level shapes fill their box; rules use their dedicated *Rule boxes, render at 1.5-2 px stroke and never cross text. Paired objects have dedicated content boxes (openCore, lyricText, stickerBed, stickerText, stickerRule, stickerBurst, stageBurst, chaseArrow, closeStrip, closeBody) so a bed, a sticker, its copy and its rule cannot collapse onto one anchor. When two ops still share a box, the higher-z op is nested inside the lower-z op and preserves its 16:9 relative inset; equal z uses composition order; nested shapes never fill the parent box. Never stretch a 16:9 composition."
    }
